NAME "The mode cycle is the sequence the reference documentation states"
WINDOW 100 30
TARGET pigasus
SETTINGS '{"agentMode":"plan","showTips":false}'

# The cycle, as a table.
#
# official-docs/cli/modes.md states it outright:
#
#     `default` > `accept-edits` > `auto` > `plan` > `default`
#     Where `auto` mode isn't available, cycling skips directly from
#     `accept-edits` to `plan`.
#
# Four stops, with default and auto as separate modes. Each stop is one row
# below, written as the two things the screen can be asked about it: the exact
# tail of the status row's right segment, and the composer's banner ("-" for
# the default stop, which names nothing). MODE_CYCLE presses shift+tab once
# per row and checks each landing against that row, so a wrong order fails on
# the stop it is wrong at and names the mode that stop should have been.
#
# The table opens and closes on `plan`: the first row is asserted without a
# press, which pins that a stored mode is honoured rather than replaced by the
# default, and the last row is the lap closing rather than a list walking off
# the end.
#
# WHY THIS IS TARGET pigasus AND NOT TARGET both
#
# agy cannot be the oracle for this on this host. Its `--mode auto` reports
# "Auto mode is not available: it needs the OS terminal sandbox and may not
# be rolled out to you yet" and falls back to default, so its cycle is the
# three-stop one the documentation describes for that case. Comparing the two
# panes would assert that a build with auto available must behave like one
# without it, which is the opposite of what we want.
#
# The invariant this scene owns is the one the documentation states for a host
# where auto IS available, which is the build we ship.
#
# WHY THE TABLE AND NOT ASSERT_NOT_TEXT
#
# A sequence is data. Writing it as "here, plan must be absent" encodes the
# expected value only by exclusion, so a cycle that skips a stop entirely, or
# visits it twice, can pass — nothing names the stop that was supposed to be
# there.

#        mode            status row's right segment           composer banner
MODE_CYCLE_ROW plan      "plan · Gemini 3.8 Flash · high"     "Plan mode: research & plan only (shift+tab to cycle)"
MODE_CYCLE_ROW default   "Gemini 3.8 Flash · high"            -
MODE_CYCLE_ROW accept-edits "accept-edits · Gemini 3.8 Flash · high" "Accept-edits mode: file edits auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)"
MODE_CYCLE_ROW auto      "auto · Gemini 3.8 Flash · high"     "Auto mode: edits & safe commands auto-approved (shift+tab to cycle)"
MODE_CYCLE_ROW plan      "plan · Gemini 3.8 Flash · high"     "Plan mode: research & plan only (shift+tab to cycle)"

BOOT_BOTH
WAIT_READY 15s

MODE_CYCLE

SNAPSHOT "01_lap_complete"

DIFF
CLEANUP
